From 9d824ae890b7d6cac36244fbe920b83578f7c334 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 13:43:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Record tile-image draws through dynamic rendering

Consume descriptor-free color tile-image metadata only with the real enabled Vulkan 1.3 dynamic-rendering and tile-color-read contract. Match whole graphics pipelines, secondary inheritance and primary rendering attachment formats, including holes and ordinary depth/stencil coattachments. Keep existing legacy paths and refuse unsupported combinations explicitly.

Record each dynamic draw in a separate instance, preserving attachment load/store and the runtime's full outside-instance dependencies. Support ordinary compatible draws and pending pipeline compilation; refuse indirect-command-buffer replay and other unimplemented instance transformations. Copy dynamic rendering and inheritance arguments into the deferred recorder, and prime the new entry points only on eligible devices.

Bump RUNTIME_VERSION to 1498 because execution and refusal behavior change. Regenerate the validation runtime source pin from the existing validation build script and update the refusal reach inventory.

Validation: 10 dynamic-filter runtime tests passed on lavapipe with the Khronos validation layer, including a real ordinary-shader execution proving two dynamic instances preserve color/depth/stencil and replay matching begin/end calls. Exact feature-enable, priming-gate and legacy inline-split/readback tests also passed (13 selected tests total). Runtime lib/test clippy passed with all features, CPU-ICD cfg and -D warnings. This does not validate tile-image instructions on hardware: lavapipe lacks that extension, and no Pixel was connected.
