+### Color framebuffer fetch through tile images
+
+Where the translator selects `VK_EXT_shader_tile_image` for a plain color framebuffer fetch,
+the runtime uses Vulkan dynamic rendering. This requires an effective Vulkan API of at least
+1.3, the extension, and both `dynamicRendering` and `shaderTileImageColorReadAccess` enabled on
+the logical device. A consumer must request at least 1.3 in `instance_api_version` on a loader
+that supports it; the default 1.2 instance cannot expose this path. An adopted device must
+likewise report its actual enabled features. The translator's existing rasterization-order
+attachment access and pixel-interlock paths keep their own render-pass contracts.
+
+Tile images occupy color attachment locations directly and use no input-attachment descriptor.
+The dynamic pipeline, the secondary command buffer's inheritance and the rendering instance
+agree on every color format and absent attachment, plus any ordinary depth/stencil attachment.
+Colors remain in `GENERAL`; depth/stencil layouts change through explicit barriers. The
+deferred command recorder copies the rendering attachments and inheritance formats before
+their callers' temporary structures go away.
+
+Each tile-reading draw currently runs in its own rendering instance, with stores and loads
+preserving attachment contents and the runtime's full barriers between instances. This avoids
+using the legacy in-pass storage and pre-rasterization barriers where dynamic rendering does
+not permit them, at the cost of a store/load boundary per draw. Compatible ordinary draws
+after a tile-reading draw continue on this route. This supports single-sample, directly
+represented float or unsigned-integer color reads, including ordinary depth/stencil tests on
+coattachments. Pipeline compilation may complete asynchronously; its secondary still inherits
+the same dynamic attachment contract.
+
+`NotImplemented(TileImageRendering)` refuses combinations whose dynamic contract is not
+implemented: multisampling, attachment resolves, multiview, remapped color locations, legacy
+input-attachment or interlocked-storage mixes, shader-side depth/stencil, fragment imageblocks,
+rasterization-rate maps, capture/rerouting, color regrouping and indirect-command-buffer replay.
+The translator separately refuses tile-read expressions whose helper-invocation behavior it
+cannot preserve. This color-read path does not provide general raster-order-group semantics.
+
